  "body": "Removes the two manual-only GitHub workflows, `ci.yml` and `nightly.yml`, and the texts that described them. Both had only a `workflow_dispatch` trigger; `ci.yml` last ran 2026-11-06, `nightly.yml` has no run in the last 100. Every gate tier runs locally (`cargo xtask gate`).\n\nFiles touched:\n- `.github/workflows/ci.yml`, `.github/workflows/nightly.yml`: deleted. `release.yml` and `aur-package.yml` are untouched and do not reference them.\n- `AGENTS.md`: \"GitHub Actions minutes are budgeted\" now says GitHub runs only `release.yml` on a pushed tag (`aur-package.yml` is a job it calls), the two files are gone (maintainer quote, 2026-11-13), and a clean-machine gate run on GitHub is issue 1413's subject.\n- `README.md`, `site/content/developers/gates.md`: drop the \"CI and nightly workflows are manual\" sentences.\n- `scripts/README.md`: gate tier table no longer says \"when run by hand\" via the deleted workflows.\n- `.claude/PROCESS_VERSION`: 54 -> 55 (AGENTS.md is a process file).\n- `docs/decisions/1415-remove-dead-workflows.md`: the decision entry.\n\nHow checked: `git grep -i \"ci\\.yml\\|nightly\\.yml\"` over the tree finds only the AGENTS.md sentence that records the removal, plus history files (CHANGELOG.md, RECOMMENDED.md, RELEASE_NOTES.md), which are left alone. `xtask/src/tests.rs` mentions \"nightly\" only as an invalid gate tier name in a parse test, unrelated. No cargo command, build, gate or test was run (a release gate was using the machine; the change is files and text only, no Rust touched). Not exercised: GitHub parsing of `release.yml` (unchanged file).\n\nChangelog: none\n\nPROCESS_VERSION 55: the two manual workflows are gone; a fork pulls the process files and may delete its own copies\n\nFixes #1415\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
